#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:6
msgid "Exercise: `Display` Derive"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:8
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will walk through the conceptual implementation of a "
"custom **`Display` derive macro** using the `syn` and `quote` crates."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:11
msgid ""
"Since we are running this in a single-file environment without a separate "
"`proc-macro = true` crate setup, we will write a normal Rust function that "
"takes simulated token streams (using `proc_macro2` and `quote!`), parses "
"them with `syn`, generates the output with `quote!`, and asserts that the "
"generated code is correct."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:17
msgid "Your task:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:19
msgid "Implement the `derive_display_impl` function to:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:21
msgid ""
"Parse the incoming token stream `input` into a `syn::DeriveInput` struct."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:22
msgid "Extract the name (identifier) of the struct."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:23
msgid ""
"Generate and return a token stream implementing `std::fmt::Display` for that "
"struct name, which formats the struct using its name, names of its fields, "
"and their values. (e.g., printing `MyAwesomeType { a: 50, }`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:27
msgid ""
"The names of the struct's fields can be obtained with the provided "
"`struct_fields` function."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:30
msgid "This will rely on a `Cargo.toml` resembling:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/proc-macros/exercise.md:32
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"proc-macro-exercise\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"publish = false\n"
"\n"
"[[bin]]\n"
"name = \"proc-macro-exercise\"\n"
"path = \"exercise.rs\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"proc-macro2 = \"1.0\"\n"
"quote = \"1.0\"\n"
"syn = \"2.0\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

